* bench_ne555: bipolar 555 timer (project-authored behavioural subcircuit from R, C, V, D and S elements).
* Ports, in DIP pin order (gn = GND pin; "gnd" would be node 0 in ngspice): gn trig out reset ctrl thr dis vcc.
* - Internal 3 x 5 kohm divider: ctrl sits at 2/3 VCC, node n13 at 1/3 VCC (CONT overrides both, as in the IC).
* - The comparators are voltage-controlled switches comparing THR with ctrl and TRIG with n13 directly.
* - SR latch: node q (0 or 1 V above gnd) is set by Sset (TRIG below n13), cleared by Srst (THR above ctrl) and held
*   by Shold, a switch controlled by q itself. Path resistances order the priorities: RESET below 0.7 V (1 ohm)
*   beats set (10 ohm), which beats clear (100 ohm), which beats hold (1 kohm). RESET has only a 1 Gohm leak to GND,
*   so an unwired RESET reads low and holds the timer in reset: tie it to VCC when unused, as the datasheet says.
* - Output: Shi (diode + 7.7 ohm from VCC) or Slo (8 ohm to gnd); discharge: Sdis (19 ohm) on while the output is low.
* - Supply: the 15 kohm divider plus 1.75 kohm gives about 3.2 mA at 5 V and 9.6 mA at 15 V.
.subckt bench_ne555 gn trig out reset ctrl thr dis vcc
.model bench_555_cmp SW(VT=0 VH=1m RON=1 ROFF=1e9)
.model bench_555_q SW(VT=0.5 VH=0.1 RON=1 ROFF=1e9)
.model bench_555_doh D(Is=1e-12 N=1.37)
Rd1 vcc ctrl 5k
Rd2 ctrl n13 5k
Rd3 n13 gn 5k
Rsup vcc gn 1.75k
Rthr thr gn 1e9
Rtrig trig gn 1e9
Rrst reset gn 1e9
Vone one gn DC 1
Vrth rth gn DC 0.7
Rq q gn 10k
Cq q gn 10p
Sset one qs n13 trig bench_555_cmp
Rqs qs q 9
Srst q rq thr ctrl bench_555_cmp
Rrq rq gn 99
Shold one qh q gn bench_555_q
Rqh qh q 999
Sres q gn rth reset bench_555_cmp
* outputs (RON of these switches is 1 ohm; the series parts complete the fitted values)
Shi vcc oh q gn bench_555_q
Dhi oh oh2 bench_555_doh
Rhi oh2 out 6.7
Slo out ol hlf q bench_555_cmp
Rlo ol gn 7
Vhlf hlf gn DC 0.5
Sdis dis dl hlf q bench_555_cmp
Rdl dl gn 18
.ends bench_ne555
